Chordify by Duphon

Chordify turns any sound into a chord. Pick notes on its keyboard, save chords into eight slots, and whatever you feed it (drums, voice, noise, pads) comes out playing that chord.

This installer can add:

  - VST3 plug-in      /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Chordify.vst3
  - Audio Unit        /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Chordify.component
  - Standalone app    /Applications/Chordify.app

Choose "Customize" on the next screens to install only some of them. Installing a newer version replaces the old one in place.

After installing, rescan plug-ins in your DAW if Chordify doesn't show up. The standalone app will ask for microphone access the first time it runs, because it processes your audio input.

To uninstall, delete the files listed above (or run the "Uninstall Chordify" script that came with this installer).
